===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|graduat|alt=graduat(e)|t=(noun) a graduate of a university; (adjective) graduate, having graduated|pos=also used as the past participle of {{m|enm|graduaten||to graduate}}}}, borrowed from {{der|en|ML.|graduātus||graduated, graduate}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|ML.|graduō||to graduate}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}}), from {{m|la|gradus||step}} + {{m|la|-ō|id=denominative|pos=verb-forming suffix}}. The noun is originally derived within Latin from the adjective via [[substantivization]], see {{af|en|-ate|id1=substantive|pos1=noun-forming suffix}}. Sense 10 of the verb, relating to Japanese entertainment, is a {{sl|en|ja|卒業|tr=sotsugyō|nocap=1}}.

